Cypress (15 and 16) helper for this template — in a Cypress suite, use it as written:
Facts:
  • hidden radio inputs, operated by their labels — click the label, assert the input
  • the inputs carry the option name in aria-label and a value ("teams" / "individuals") in name="plan_type_selector"
  • assert the input's selected state, not that it exists (it is hidden)
```js
const planTypeInput = (option) =>
  cy.get('input[name="plan_type_selector"]')
    .should(($all) => expect($all.filter(`[aria-label="${option}"]`), `plan type "${option}" on the page`).to.have.length(1))
    .then(($all) => $all.filter(`[aria-label="${option}"]`));
// The radios are hidden: click the visible label, then wait for the input to be checked.
const selectPlanType = (option) => {
  planTypeInput(option).invoke('attr', 'id').then((id) => cy.get(`label[for="${id}"]`).click());
  planTypeInput(option).should('be.checked');
};
```
